  "prefLabel": "Agr 908.01 Purpose",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Agr 908.01 Purpose. The rules in this part implement the procedures of the department of agriculture, markets, and food, pursuant to RSA 426:18-20, allowing builders in municipalities that regulate the use of native lumber to use native lumber without the stamp of a grading agency when the lumber is graded and certified by a grader employed by a New Hampshire wood processing mill.\n\nSource. #6171, eff 1-24-96, EXPIRED: 1-24-04\n\nNew. #14550, eff 4-1-26, EXPIRES: 4-1-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/agr900.html"
}
